# Transitive dependency of caddy:alpine (the runtime image we use).
# Upstream Caddy has migrated its direct dependency to go-jose v4, but
# something still pulls v3.0.4 into the final binary. Tracking until
# Caddy releases an image with go-jose/v3 >= v3.0.5.
#
# Not exploitable in our deployment: the blog serves static files only;
# the JOSE code path is not reached at runtime.
CVE-2026-34986

# Go stdlib (net/http, crypto/tls) vulnerabilities baked into the caddy:alpine
# runtime image, which still ships Go 1.26.8 as of 2026-10-09. Fixed upstream
# in Go 1.26.9/1.27.2, but Caddy's official image hasn't been rebuilt against
# it yet. Both are DoS-only (no RCE/data exposure); this blog is a static
# site with no sensitive data or availability SLA. Drop once caddy:alpine
# picks up the patched Go toolchain.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031
